1038 #edb/ref 17592186351257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133785 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186394133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133785 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186394140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133785 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186417869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133785 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186417872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133785 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186480653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133785 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186480687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133785 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector onto the Solution Space of a System of Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133785 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186133594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133785 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f8d8c7fb-e69a-5b52-9566-4d2e0c7e54fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134001 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134001 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134001 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134001 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134001 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186134670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134001 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134001 #edb/ref 1045 "Projecting Vectors Onto One-Dimensional Subspaces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134001 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186134666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134001 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134001 #edb/ref 1050 840.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134001 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "c533ceb7-ea46-55fe-9613-b36245be3181" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134288 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134288 #edb/ref 1069 "q-40425" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134288 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134288 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134288 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c185f4ac-1057-5248-8964-7fb26d1dea03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134288 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{2}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 1}{{(-1)}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-8}{2}b \\\\  & =-4b \\\\  & =-4[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134666 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134666 #edb/ref 1061 20237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134666 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "102b1c5a-b877-5357-9263-23e920a24266" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134666 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186135046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134667 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134667 #edb/ref 1061 20238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134667 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b35849c7-639b-5885-a390-1bb6cfee6fb9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134667 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134668 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134668 #edb/ref 1061 20239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134668 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7e646647-d2d1-5d2a-9a95-42a1ab8c82db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134668 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186135047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134669 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134669 #edb/ref 1061 20240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134669 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "01e8aa19-ae85-5957-bee9-f3c3292381c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134669 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134670 #edb/ref 1061 20241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134670 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b86ddd36-bd23-56a6-b22f-b78dbd8d1d6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134670 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135046 #edb/ref 1064 "The **orthogonal projection** of a vector $\\mathbf{x}$ onto a span $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ is the vector in $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ that is \"closest\" to $\\mathbf{x}.$ Let's work an example to clarify what we mean by \"closest.\"\n\nConsider the following two vectors:\n\n![](images/00/0079b00022e2f536fc3cc60db20657be10024ed81bcca3f802d2b25d8072c0ce.svg) \n\nGeometrically, $\\mathbf{x}$ can be written as the sum of a vector $k{\\mathbf{a}}$ that lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ and \nanother vector $\\mathbf{z}$ that belongs to the orthogonal complement of $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$, as illustrated in the picture below.\n\n![](images/a4/a4754bf048aa6c05cd7ef574af306150c30d435f90afec36f492ed4b8013e899.png)\n\nThe vector $k\\mathbf a$ is called the **orthogonal projection** of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ as the sum\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = k \\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{z},\n$$\n\nfor some $k \\in \\mathbb{R}$ and ${\\mathbf{z}} \\perp \\mathbf{a}.$ \n\nTo compute the orthogonal projection $k \\mathbf{a},$ we can first find the dot product of both sides of the equation above with $\\mathbf{a}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot a & =(ka+z)\\cdot a \\\\ x\\cdot a & =k(a\\cdot a)+z\\cdot a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{z},$ we have $\\mathbf{z} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} = 0.$ As a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot a & =k(a\\cdot a) \\\\ k & =\\frac{x\\cdot a}{a\\cdot a} \\\\ k & =\\frac{5\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot (-6)+0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 6}{{3}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the orthogonal projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ka=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** There is a shortcut! Instead of going through this process each time, we can compute the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}\\,a\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135046 #edb/ref 1065 3622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135046 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8c57e0ac-99f7-5b01-ace0-7afa2449f0af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135046 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135047 #edb/ref 1064 "We define the **distance** between the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and the vector space $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ to be\n\n$$\n\\Vert \\mathbf{x} - \\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{a}}\\,\\mathbf{x} \\Vert.\n$$\n\nWe can also define the **angle** $\\theta$ between the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and the subspace $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ to be the acute angle between the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and its orthogonal projection $\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{a}}\\,\\mathbf{x},$ as shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/a2/a2a2670a6df46d3cac249b5c84b960c3877542be0dc656ad64840ef42ce025c4.png)\n\nFinally, we now can represent the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ as a sum of two orthogonal vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = \\underbrace{\\textrm{proj}_{\\mathbf{a}}\\mathbf{x}}_{\\large \\mathbf{y}} + \\underbrace{(\\mathbf{x}-\\textrm{proj}_{\\mathbf{a}}\\mathbf{x})}_{\\large \\mathbf{z}},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{y} \\in \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}$ and $\\mathbf{z} \\perp \\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}.$\n\n**Note:** The vector $\\textbf{x}-\\textrm{proj}_{\\mathbf{a}}\\mathbf{x},$ whose norm $\\| \\textbf{x}-\\textrm{proj}_{\\mathbf{a}}\\mathbf{x} \\|$ represents the distance from $\\mathbf{x}$ to $\\mathbf{a},$ is sometimes called the **vector rejection of $\\mathbf{x}$ from $\\mathbf{a}.$**" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135047 #edb/ref 1065 3623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135047 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "05384c2f-78e1-513a-a296-5a9a856a6652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135047 #edb/ref 1067 "The Distance  Between a Vector and a One-Dimensional Subspace" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324172 #edb/ref 1080 "3\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324172 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324172 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "16a1e738-b3ef-5617-b65b-5d1f78a95729" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324529 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324529 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324529 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "45044c73-09fa-58fb-ae57-8c07fb707cfa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324826 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324826 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324826 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "667e35b4-0791-5c90-8a77-80282219a6bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325144 #edb/ref 1080 "3\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325144 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325144 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "89c9f2ab-6dfa-5033-9188-0d8f7909b792" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325310 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325310 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325310 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9dea4603-4170-5303-b0d8-6e693ae1d694" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325332 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325332 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325332 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a070fc81-cb3f-5111-b4d2-2fc2ca2fcb13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325500 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325500 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325500 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b26dd048-2cb5-50ad-b8cc-18bbc89f309d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325675 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325675 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325675 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c5916d48-938f-526e-8328-76ddea847a8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325695 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325695 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325695 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c747df10-7018-5c0d-8076-0f5bb121d072" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325706 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325706 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325706 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c8339040-d0af-5ec3-87ec-5da28e3ea2d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186324529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186324826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326261 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326261 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326261 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186325310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326261 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "172eecd4-ca09-54f5-ab2c-6aae53cb47da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326618 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186324172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326618 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326618 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326618 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326618 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326618 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326618 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326618 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186325332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326618 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "db70c3b6-c34e-5eef-8233-7d0b5498da99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326840 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326840 #edb/ref 1069 "q-40411" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326840 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326840 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the distance between $x$ and $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326840 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "334df9d1-dd1e-5b54-85c8-f150ef338d78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326840 #edb/ref 1074 "The distance between the vector $x$ and the vector space $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}$ is given by $‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖$, where $\\overset{^}{x}$ in the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{span}\\{b\\}.$\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{b\\cdot x}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-2)+(-1)(-2)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-2-2+2}{1+1+1+1}b \\\\  & =-b \\\\  & =-1[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{((-2)-(-1))^{2}+(2-1)^{2}+((-2)-(-1))^{2}+((-2)-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394140 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186394141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394140 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81200" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394140 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394140 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394140 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8bc5c35e-337a-5a6f-8888-1b0686935cc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394140 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find a basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3\\cdot (2{x}_{3})=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=6{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 6+5\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 1}{{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{82}{41}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394141 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394141 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394141 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394141 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394141 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394141 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394141 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394141 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186394145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394141 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4e0e70c3-1109-58cb-a447-88acb9d0e5b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394142 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394142 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17