{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3\\cdot (2{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=5{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 5+(-5)\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot 1}{{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-60\\,}{\\,\\,\\,30\\,}b \\\\  & =-2b \\\\  & =-2[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417871 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417871 #edb/ref 1069 "q-40381" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417871 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417871 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ If $x=y+z,$ where $y\\in \\text{Span}\\{a\\}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}\\{a\\},$ then $z=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417871 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3365c089-bf35-5299-ad47-d460e03b5d34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417871 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/d8/d887852fe51f08cb7296437e69b6a9632721cfd155558e6abf9a99b4f59f7ad6.png)\n\nFirst, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{a\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x & =\\frac{a\\cdot x}{a\\cdot a}a \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 7+(-3)(-6)+1\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{6+21+18+1}{4+9+9+1}a \\\\  & =\\frac{46}{23}a \\\\  & =2a \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ z & =x-{\\text{proj}}_{a}\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $y\\in \\text{Span}\\{a\\}$ and $z⊥\\text{Span}\\{a\\},$ as shown in the picture above.\n\nIn conclusion, $z=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417873 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417873 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "62a4d3df-d96d-5ff1-bcdc-6b9572844deb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417873 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417874 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417874 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7d14fc8b-c658-5579-8cfd-ea6f41729396" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417874 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417875 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417875 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "962d37cc-84fe-5f22-9f18-fe787b5d8f8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417875 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417876 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bdf29d7e-7c25-5367-b984-2503f598b196" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417876 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417877 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417877 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c8ab4513-610d-50c5-a113-b2b14f2cbf31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417877 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428638 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436